{"surah": 89, "verses": [{"ayah": 1, "text": "وَٱلْفَجْرِ ", "translation": "By the dawn", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَٱلْفَجْرِ", "translit": "ِrْjgَfْlٱَw", "root": "فجر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 2, "text": "وَلَيَالٍ عَشْرٍ ", "translation": "And [by] ten nights[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلَيَالٍ", "translit": "ٍlāَyَlَw", "root": "ليل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَشْرٍ", "translit": "ٍrْhsَʿع", "root": "عشر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 3, "text": "وَٱلشَّفْعِ وَٱلْوَتْرِ ", "translation": "And [by] the even [number] and the odd", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَٱلشَّفْعِ", "translit": "ِʿعْfَّhslٱَw", "root": "شفع"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "وَٱلْوَتْرِ", "translit": "ِrْtَwْlٱَw", "root": "وتر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 4, "text": "وَٱلَّيْلِ إِذَا يَسْرِ ", "translation": "And [by] the night when it passes,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَٱلَّيْلِ", "translit": "ِlْyَّlٱَw", "root": "ليل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "يَسْرِ", "translit": "ِrْsَy", "root": "سري"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 5, "text": "هَلْ فِى ذَٰلِكَ قَسَمٌ لِّذِى حِجْرٍ ", "translation": "Is there [not] in [all] that an oath [sufficient] for one of perception?[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "هَلْ", "translit": "ْlَh", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhd", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "قَسَمٌ", "translit": "ٌmَsَq", "root": "قسم"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "لِّذِى", "translit": "àِhdِّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "حِجْرٍ", "translit": "ٍrْjgِḥ", "root": "حجر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 6, "text": "أَلَمْ تَرَ كَيْفَ فَعَلَ رَبُّكَ بِعَادٍ ", "translation": "Have you not considered how your Lord dealt with ʿAad -", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَلَمْ", "translit": "ْmَlَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "تَرَ", "translit": "َrَt", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "كَيْفَ", "translit": "َfْyَk", "root": "كيف"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فَعَلَ", "translit": "َlَʿعَf", "root": "فعل"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "رَبُّكَ", "translit": "َkُّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "بِعَادٍ", "translit": "ٍdāَʿعِb", "root": "عود"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 7, "text": "إِرَمَ ذَاتِ ٱلْعِمَادِ ", "translation": "[With] Iram[1] - who had lofty pillars,[2]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِرَمَ", "translit": "َmَrِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ذَاتِ", "translit": "ِtāَhd", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْعِمَادِ", "translit": "ِdāَmِʿعْlٱ", "root": "عمد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 8, "text": "ٱلَّتِى لَمْ يُخْلَقْ مِثْلُهَا فِى ٱلْبِلَٰدِ ", "translation": "The likes of whom had never been created in the land?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ٱلَّتِى", "translit": "àِtَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَمْ", "translit": "ْmَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "يُخْلَقْ", "translit": "ْqَlْhkُy", "root": "خلق"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مِثْلُهَا", "translit": "āَhُlْhtِm", "root": "مثل"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلْبِلَٰدِ", "translit": "ِdَٰlِbْlٱ", "root": "بلد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 9, "text": "وَثَمُودَ ٱلَّذِينَ جَابُوا۟ ٱلصَّخْرَ بِٱلْوَادِ ", "translation": "And [with] Thamūd, who carved out the rocks in the valley?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَثَمُودَ", "translit": "َdwُmَhtَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "جَابُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُbāَjg", "root": "جوب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلصَّخْرَ", "translit": "َrْhkَّṣlٱ", "root": "صخر"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "بِٱلْوَادِ", "translit": "ِdāَwْlٱِb", "root": "ودي"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 10, "text": "وَفِرْعَوْنَ ذِى ٱلْأَوْتَادِ ", "translation": "And [with] Pharaoh, owner of the stakes?[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَفِرْعَوْنَ", "translit": "َnْwَʿعْrِfَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ذِى", "translit": "àِhd", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْأَوْتَادِ", "translit": "ِdāَtْwَaʾْlٱ", "root": "وتد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 11, "text": "ٱلَّذِينَ طَغَوْا۟ فِى ٱلْبِلَٰدِ ", "translation": "[All of] whom oppressed within the lands", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "طَغَوْا۟", "translit": "۟āْwَغَṭ", "root": "طغي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْبِلَٰدِ", "translit": "ِdَٰlِbْlٱ", "root": "بلد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 12, "text": "فَأَكْثَرُوا۟ فِيهَا ٱلْفَسَادَ ", "translation": "And increased therein the corruption.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَأَكْثَرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrَhtْkَaʾَf", "root": "كثر"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "فِيهَا", "translit": "āَhyِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْفَسَادَ", "translit": "َdāَsَfْlٱ", "root": "فسد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 13, "text": "فَصَبَّ عَلَيْهِمْ رَبُّكَ سَوْطَ عَذَابٍ ", "translation": "So your Lord poured upon them a scourge of punishment.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَصَبَّ", "translit": "َّbَṣَf", "root": "صبب"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "رَبُّكَ", "translit": "َkُّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "سَوْطَ", "translit": "َṭْwَs", "root": "سوط"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "عَذَابٍ", "translit": "ٍbāَhdَʿع", "root": "عذب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 14, "text": "إِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَبِٱلْمِرْصَادِ ", "translation": "Indeed, your Lord is in observation.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "رَبَّكَ", "translit": "َkَّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَبِٱلْمِرْصَادِ", "translit": "ِdāَṣْrِmْlٱِbَl", "root": "رصد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 15, "text": "فَأَمَّا ٱلْإِنسَٰنُ إِذَا مَا ٱبْتَلَىٰهُ رَبُّهُۥ فَأَكْرَمَهُۥ وَنَعَّمَهُۥ فَيَقُولُ رَبِّىٓ أَكْرَمَنِ ", "translation": "And as for man, when his Lord tries him and [thus] is generous to him and favors him, he says, \"My Lord has honored me.\"[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَأَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَaʾَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْإِنسَٰنُ", "translit": "ُnَٰsnِiʾْlٱ", "root": "انس"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱبْتَلَىٰهُ", "translit": "ُhٰàَlَtْbٱ", "root": "بلو"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "رَبُّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhُّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "فَأَكْرَمَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَmَrْkَaʾَf", "root": "كرم"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَنَعَّمَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَmَّʿعَnَw", "root": "نعم"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "فَيَقُولُ", "translit": "ُlwُqَyَf", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "رَبِّىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "أَكْرَمَنِ", "translit": "ِnَmَrْkَaʾ", "root": "كرم"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 16, "text": "وَأَمَّآ إِذَا مَا ٱبْتَلَىٰهُ فَقَدَرَ عَلَيْهِ رِزْقَهُۥ فَيَقُولُ رَبِّىٓ أَهَٰنَنِ ", "translation": "But when He tries him and restricts his provision, he says, \"My Lord has humiliated me.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَأَمَّآ", "translit": "ٓāَّmَaʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱبْتَلَىٰهُ", "translit": "ُhٰàَlَtْbٱ", "root": "بلو"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "فَقَدَرَ", "translit": "َrَdَqَf", "root": "قدر"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "رِزْقَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَqْzِr", "root": "رزق"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "فَيَقُولُ", "translit": "ُlwُqَyَf", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "رَبِّىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "أَهَٰنَنِ", "translit": "ِnَnَٰhَaʾ", "root": "هون"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 17, "text": "كَلَّاۖ بَل لَّا تُكْرِمُونَ ٱلْيَتِيمَ ", "translation": "No![1] But you do not honor the orphan", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "كَلَّا", "translit": "āَّlَk", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بَل", "translit": "lَb", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَّا", "translit": "āَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "تُكْرِمُونَ", "translit": "َnwُmِrْkُt", "root": "كرم"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْيَتِيمَ", "translit": "َmyِtَyْlٱ", "root": "يتم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 18, "text": "وَلَا تَحَٰٓضُّونَ عَلَىٰ طَعَامِ ٱلْمِسْكِينِ ", "translation": "And you do not encourage one another to feed the poor.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "تَحَٰٓضُّونَ", "translit": "َnwُّḍَٰٓḥَt", "root": "حضض"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "طَعَامِ", "translit": "ِmāَʿعَṭ", "root": "طعم"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْمِسْكِينِ", "translit": "ِnyِkْsِmْlٱ", "root": "سكن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 19, "text": "وَتَأْكُلُونَ ٱلتُّرَاثَ أَكْلًا لَّمًّا ", "translation": "And you consume inheritance, devouring [it] altogether,[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَتَأْكُلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlُkْaʾَtَw", "root": "اكل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلتُّرَاثَ", "translit": "َhtāَrُّtlٱ", "root": "ورث"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَكْلًا", "translit": "āًlْkَaʾ", "root": "اكل"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَّمًّا", "translit": "āًّmَّl", "root": "لمم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 20, "text": "وَتُحِبُّونَ ٱلْمَالَ حُبًّا جَمًّا ", "translation": "And you love wealth with immense love.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَتُحِبُّونَ", "translit": "َnwُّbِḥُtَw", "root": "حبب"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْمَالَ", "translit": "َlāَmْlٱ", "root": "مول"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "حُبًّا", "translit": "āًّbُḥ", "root": "حبب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "جَمًّا", "translit": "āًّmَjg", "root": "جمم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 21, "text": "كَلَّآ إِذَا دُكَّتِ ٱلْأَرْضُ دَكًّا دَكًّا ", "translation": "No! When the earth has been leveled - pounded and crushed", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "كَلَّآ", "translit": "ٓāَّlَk", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "دُكَّتِ", "translit": "ِtَّkُd", "root": "دكك"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْأَرْضُ", "translit": "ُḍْrَaʾْlٱ", "root": "ارض"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "دَكًّا", "translit": "āًّkَd", "root": "دكك"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "دَكًّا", "translit": "āًّkَd", "root": "دكك"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 22, "text": "وَجَآءَ رَبُّكَ وَٱلْمَلَكُ صَفًّا صَفًّا ", "translation": "And your Lord has come[1] and the angels, rank upon rank,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَجَآءَ", "translit": "َءٓāَjgَw", "root": "جيا"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "رَبُّكَ", "translit": "َkُّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَٱلْمَلَكُ", "translit": "ُkَlَmْlٱَw", "root": "ملك"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "صَفًّا", "translit": "āًّfَṣ", "root": "صفف"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "صَفًّا", "translit": "āًّfَṣ", "root": "صفف"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 23, "text": "وَجِا۟ىٓءَ يَوْمَئِذٍۭ بِجَهَنَّمَۚ يَوْمَئِذٍ يَتَذَكَّرُ ٱلْإِنسَٰنُ وَأَنَّىٰ لَهُ ٱلذِّكْرَىٰ ", "translation": "And brought [within view], that Day, is Hell - that Day, man will remember, but how [i.e., what good] to him will be the remembrance?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَجِا۟ىٓءَ", "translit": "َءٓà۟āِjgَw", "root": "جيا"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَوْمَئِذٍۭ", "translit": "ٍۭhdِyʾَmْwَy", "root": "يوم"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بِجَهَنَّمَ", "translit": "َmَّnَhَjgِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يَوْمَئِذٍ", "translit": "ٍhdِyʾَmْwَy", "root": "يوم"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "يَتَذَكَّرُ", "translit": "ُrَّkَhdَtَy", "root": "ذكر"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلْإِنسَٰنُ", "translit": "ُnَٰsnِiʾْlٱ", "root": "انس"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَأَنَّىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَّnَaʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "لَهُ", "translit": "ُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱلذِّكْرَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَrْkِّhdlٱ", "root": "ذكر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 24, "text": "يَقُولُ يَٰلَيْتَنِى قَدَّمْتُ لِحَيَاتِى ", "translation": "He will say, \"Oh, I wish I had sent ahead [some good] for my life.\"[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "يَقُولُ", "translit": "ُlwُqَy", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَٰلَيْتَنِى", "translit": "àِnَtْyَlَٰy", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "قَدَّمْتُ", "translit": "ُtْmَّdَq", "root": "قدم"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لِحَيَاتِى", "translit": "àِtāَyَḥِl", "root": "حيي"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 25, "text": "فَيَوْمَئِذٍ لَّا يُعَذِّبُ عَذَابَهُۥٓ أَحَدٌ ", "translation": "So on that Day, none will punish [as severely] as His punishment,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَيَوْمَئِذٍ", "translit": "ٍhdِyʾَmْwَyَf", "root": "يوم"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَّا", "translit": "āَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "يُعَذِّبُ", "translit": "ُbِّhdَʿعُy", "root": "عذب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "عَذَابَهُۥٓ", "translit": "ٓۥُhَbāَhdَʿع", "root": "عذب"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَحَدٌ", "translit": "ٌdَḥَaʾ", "root": "احد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 26, "text": "وَلَا يُوثِقُ وَثَاقَهُۥٓ أَحَدٌ ", "translation": "And none will bind [as severely] as His binding [of the evildoers].", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يُوثِقُ", "translit": "ُqِhtwُy", "root": "وثق"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَثَاقَهُۥٓ", "translit": "ٓۥُhَqāَhtَw", "root": "وثق"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَحَدٌ", "translit": "ٌdَḥَaʾ", "root": "احد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 27, "text": "يَٰٓأَيَّتُهَا ٱلنَّفْسُ ٱلْمُطْمَئِنَّةُ ", "translation": "[To the righteous it will be said], \"O reassured soul,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "يَٰٓأَيَّتُهَا", "translit": "āَhُtَّyَaʾَٰٓy", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلنَّفْسُ", "translit": "ُsْfَّnlٱ", "root": "نفس"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْمُطْمَئِنَّةُ", "translit": "ُẗَّnِyʾَmْṭُmْlٱ", "root": "طمان"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 28, "text": "ٱرْجِعِىٓ إِلَىٰ رَبِّكِ رَاضِيَةً مَّرْضِيَّةً ", "translation": "Return to your Lord, well-pleased and pleasing [to Him],", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ٱرْجِعِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِʿعِjgْrٱ", "root": "رجع"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "رَبِّكِ", "translit": "ِkِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "رَاضِيَةً", "translit": "ًẗَyِḍāَr", "root": "رضو"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مَّرْضِيَّةً", "translit": "ًẗَّyِḍْrَّm", "root": "رضو"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 29, "text": "فَٱدْخُلِى فِى عِبَٰدِى ", "translation": "And enter among My [righteous] servants", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَٱدْخُلِى", "translit": "àِlُhkْdٱَf", "root": "دخل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عِبَٰدِى", "translit": "àِdَٰbِʿع", "root": "عبد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 30, "text": "وَٱدْخُلِى جَنَّتِى ", "translation": "And enter My Paradise.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَٱدْخُلِى", "translit": "àِlُhkْdٱَw", "root": "دخل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "جَنَّتِى", "translit": "àِtَّnَjg", "root": "جنن"}], "hasIhya": false}], "tafsir": {"6": [{"arabic": "وهذه القصص وردت في القرآن لتعرف بها سنة الله في عباده الذي خلوا من قبل، فما في القرآن شيء إلا وهو هدى ونور وتعرف من الله تعالى إلى خلقه، فتارة يتعرف إليهم بالتقديس فيقول: \" قل هو الله أحد الله الصمد لم يلد ولم يولد ولم يكن له كفواً أحد \" وتارة يتعرف إليهم بصفات جلاله فيقول: \" الملك القدوس السلام المؤمن المهيمن العزيز الجبار المتكبر \" وتارة يتعرف إليهم في أفعاله المخوفة والمرجوة فيتلو عليهم سنته في أعدائه وفي أنبيائه فيقول: \" ألم تر كيف فعل ربك بعاد إرم ذات العماد - ألم تر كيف فعل ربك بأصحاب الفي", "english": "And these stories came in the Quran to know through them the Way (Sunnah) of Allah in His servants who passed before. There is nothing in the Quran except that it is guidance and light and recognition from Allah the Exalted to His creation. Sometimes He makes Himself known to them through Sanctification (Taqdis) when He says: \"Say: He is Allah, the One, Allah the Eternal Refuge. He neither begets nor is born, nor is there to Him any equivalent.\" And sometimes He makes Himself known to them through His attributes of Majesty (Jalal) when He says: \"The Sovereign, the Holy, the Peace, the Faithful, the Overseer, the Exalted in Might, the Compeller, the Superior.\" And sometimes He makes Himself known to them in His fearful and hoped-for actions, and He recites to them His Way (Sunnah) with His enemies and with His prophets when He says: \"Have you not seen how your Lord dealt with 'Aad - Iram of the pillars? Have you not seen how your Lord dealt with the companions of the elephant?\"", "book_file": "vol4_Vol4-book6.doc.txt", "book_title": "Love, Longing, Intimacy and Contentment", "content_type": "dhikr", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on the virtue and practice of remembering God, from 'Love, Longing, Intimacy and Contentment'", "badge": "Dhikr"}], "15": [{"arabic": "وكان أرباب البصائر إذا أقبلت عليهم الدنيا حزنوا وقالوا: ذنب عجلت عقوبته ورأوا ذلك علامة المقت والإهمال، وإذا أقبل عليهم الفقر قالوا: مرحباً بشعار الصالحين. والمغرور إذا أقبلت عليه الدنيا ظن أنها كرامة من الله، وإذا صرفت عنه ظن أنها هوان، كما أخبر الله تعالى عنه إذ قال \"فأما الإنسان إذا ما ابتلاه ربه فأكرمه ونعمه فيقول ربي أكرمن وأما إذا ما ابتلاه فقدر عليه رزقه فيقول ربي أهانن\" فأجاب الله عن ذلك \"كلا\" أي ليس كما قال إنما هو ابتلاء نعوذ بالله من شر البلاء ونسأل الله التثبيت، فبين أن ذلك غرور. قال", "english": "And the possessors of insight (أرباب البصائر) when the worldly life (الدنيا) approached them, they would grieve and say: 'A sin whose punishment has been hastened,' and they saw that as a sign of contempt and neglect. And when poverty approached them, they would say: 'Welcome to the emblem of the righteous.' And the deluded one (المغرور) when the worldly life approaches him, he thinks it is an honor from Allah, and when it is diverted from him, he thinks it is humiliation, as Allah the Exalted informed about him when He said: 'So as for man when his Lord tests him and honors him and bestows favor upon him, he says: My Lord has honored me. And as for when He tests him and restricts his provision, he says: My Lord has humiliated me.' So Allah responded to that with 'No' (كلا), meaning it is not as he said; rather it is a test—we seek refuge in Allah from the evil of the test and we ask Allah for steadfastness—thus He clarified that this is delusion. Al-Hasan said: He denied them both with His saying 'No' (كلا), saying: 'This is not My honoring, nor is this My humiliation. But the honored one is whom I have honored with My obedience, whether rich or poor, and the humiliated one is whom I have humiliated with My disobedience, whether rich or poor.'", "book_file": "vol3_Vol3-book-10a.doc.txt", "book_title": "Condemnation of Delusion", "content_type": "ethics", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on the diseases of the heart and their cure, from 'Condemnation of Delusion'", "badge": "Ethics"}], "27": [{"arabic": "المعنى الثاني هي اللطيفة التي ذكرناها التي هي الإنسان بالحقيقة وهي نفس الإنسان وذاته ولكنها توصف بأوصاف مختلفة بحسب اختلاف أحوالها فإذا سكنت تحت الأمر وزايلها الاضطراب بسبب معارضة الشهوات سميت النفس المطمئنة قال الله تعالى في مثلها يا أيتها النفس المطمئنة ارجعي إلى ربك راضية مرضية والنفس بالمعنى الأول لا يتصور رجوعها إلى الله تعالى فإنها مبعدة عن الله وهي من حزب الشيطان وإذا لم يتم سكونها ولكنها صارت مدافعة للنفس الشهوانية ومعترضة عليها سميت النفس اللوامة لأنها تلوم صاحبها عند تقصيره في عبادة مو", "english": "The second meaning is the subtle essence (Lafīfa) that we mentioned, which is the human being in reality, and it is the soul (Nafs) of the human being and their essence (Dhāt). However, it is described with different attributes according to the variation of its states. If it settles under the command (Amr) and disturbance leaves it due to opposing desires (Shahawāt), it is called the tranquil soul (Nafs al-Muṭmaʾinna). Allah the Exalted said regarding its example: 'O tranquil soul (Nafs al-Muṭmaʾinna), return to your Lord, well-pleased and well-pleasing.' And the soul (Nafs) in the first meaning cannot be conceived as returning to Allah the Exalted, for it is distanced from Allah and is from the party of Satan (Shayṭān). If its settling is not complete, but it becomes resistant to the desiring soul (Nafs al-Shahwāniyya) and objects to it, it is called the blaming soul (Nafs al-Lawwāma) because it blames its owner when they fall short in worshiping their Master (Mawlā). Allah the Exalted said: 'And I swear by the blaming soul (Nafs al-Lawwāma).' And if it abandons objection and submits and obeys the demands of desires (Shahawāt) and the incitements of Satan (Shayṭān), it is called the soul that commands to evil (Nafs al-Ammāra bi-l-Sūʾ). Allah the Exalted said, informing about Joseph, peace be upon him: 'Or the wife of al-ʿAzīz, and I do not acquit myself. Indeed, the soul (Nafs) commands to evil (Ammāra bi-l-Sūʾ).' And it may be permissible to say that what is intended by 'commands to evil' is the soul (Nafs) in the first meaning. Therefore, the soul (Nafs) in the first meaning is blameworthy to the utmost blame, and in the second meaning it is praiseworthy because it is the soul (Nafs) of the human being, meaning their essence (Dhāt) and reality (Ḥaqīqa), knowing Allah the Exalted and all other known things.", "book_file": "vol3_j3-k01.doc.txt", "book_title": "Disciplining the Soul", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Disciplining the Soul'", "badge": "Insight"}, {"arabic": "الواصلون الى هذه الرتبة هم الأقلون فلا جرم هم الصديقون المقربون الذين قالوا ربنا الله ثم استقاموا فهؤلاء لازموا الطريق المستقيم واستووا على الصراط القويم واطمأنت نفوسهم على مقتضى باعث الدين وإياهم ينادي المنادي ﴿ يا أيتها النفس المطمئنة ارجعي الى ربك راضية مرضية ﴾ {}.", "english": "Those who reach this rank are the fewest, so they are the Truthful Ones (Siddiqun) and the Brought-Near Ones (Muqarrabun) who said, 'Our Lord is Allah,' then remained steadfast. These have adhered to the Straight Path (Tariq al-Mustaqim) and have become firmly established on the Right Path (Sirat al-Qawim), and their Souls (Nafs) have become tranquil (Mutma'innah) upon the dictates of the religious impulse. It is to them that the Caller calls: 'O tranquil Soul (Nafs al-Mutma'innah), return to your Lord, well-pleased and well-pleasing.'", "book_file": "vol4_Vol4-book2.doc.txt", "book_title": "Patience and Gratitude", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Patience and Gratitude'", "badge": "Insight"}, {"arabic": "وسمع رجل من أهل التصوف قارئا يقرأ يا أيتها النفس المطمئنة ارجعي إلى ربك راضية مرضية فاستعادها من القارىء وقال كم أقول لها ارجعي وليست ترجع وتواجد وزعق زعقة فخرجت روحه", "english": "And a man from the people of Sufism heard a reciter reciting: 'O you Soul (Nafs) at peace (Mutma'innah), return to your Lord (Rabb), well-pleased (Radiyah) and well-pleasing (Mardiyyah).' He asked the reciter to repeat it and said: 'How many times do I say to it: Return! And it does not return.' And he experienced spiritual ecstasy (Tawajud) and let out a cry (Za'qah), then his spirit (Ruh) departed.", "book_file": "vol2_j2-k08.doc.txt", "book_title": "Audition and Ecstasy", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Audition and Ecstasy'", "badge": "Insight"}, {"arabic": "وهو القلب الذي أقبل الله عز وجل بوجهه عليه وهو القلب المطمئن المراد بقوله تعالى ألا بذكر الله تطمئن القلوب وبقوله عز وجل يا أيتها النفس المطمئنة", "english": "And it is the Heart (Qalb) that Allah the Exalted has turned His Face toward, and it is the Tranquil Heart (Qalb al-Mutma'inn) intended by His saying the Exalted: 'Indeed, in the Remembrance (Dhikr) of Allah do hearts find tranquility' and by His saying the Exalted: 'O you Tranquil Soul (Nafs al-Mutma'innah)'.", "book_file": "vol3_j3-k01.doc.txt", "book_title": "Disciplining the Soul", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Disciplining the Soul'", "badge": "Insight"}], "28": [{"arabic": "ولما كانت العقول التى بها يحصل التكليف وبها تدرك مصالح الدنيا عقولا قاصرة عن ملاحظة كنه هذا الأمر لم يأذن الله تعالى لرسول ﭬ أن يتحدث عنه بل أمره أن يكلم الناس على قدر عقولهم ولم يذكر الله تعالى في كتابه من حقيقة هذا الأمر شيئا ولكن ذكر نسبته وفعله ولم يذكر ذاته أما نسبته ففى قوله تعالى: ﴿ من أمر ربى ﴾ {} وأما فعله فقد ذكر في قوله تعالى: ﴿ ياأيها النفس المطمئنة ارجعى إلى ربك راضية مرضية فادخلى في عبادى وادخلى جنتى ﴾ {} ولنرجع الآن إلى الغرض فإن المقصود ذكر نعم الله تعالى في الأكل فقد ذكرنا بعض ن", "english": "And since the intellects (Aql) through which religious obligation (Taklif) occurs and through which worldly benefits are perceived are intellects deficient in observing the essence (Kunh) of this matter, Allah the Exalted did not permit His Messenger (peace be upon him) to speak about it, rather He commanded him to speak to people according to the capacity of their intellects. And Allah the Exalted did not mention in His Book anything of the reality (Haqiqah) of this matter, but He mentioned its attribution (Nisbah) and its action (Fi'l), and did not mention its essence (Dhat). As for its attribution, it is in His saying the Exalted: 'From the command of my Lord' (Quran 17:85). And as for its action, it has been mentioned in His saying the Exalted: 'O Soul (Nafs) at peace (Mutma'innah), return to your Lord, well-pleased (Radiyah) and well-pleasing (Mardhiyyah). Then enter among My servants, and enter My Paradise' (Quran 89:27-30). And let us now return to the purpose, for the intended is mentioning the blessings (Ni'am) of Allah the Exalted in eating, and we have mentioned some of the blessings of Allah the Exalted in the instruments of eating.", "book_file": "vol4_Vol4-book2.doc.txt", "book_title": "Patience and Gratitude", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Patience and Gratitude'", "badge": "Insight"}]}, "wordTiming": {"abdulbasit": {"1": [[1, 250, 1641]], "2": [[1, 250, 1